<title>USA: Time Warner units EBITDA up double-digits.</title>
<headline>Time Warner units EBITDA up double-digits.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc on Wednesday reported that its Time Inc, Warner Bros, HBO and Time Warner Cable all posted double-digit EBITDA increases.</p>
<p>Earlier in the day Time Warner Inc and Time Warner Entertainment Co LP reported record combined (EBITDA) earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization of $964 million on revenues of $4.877 billion for the third quarter.</p>
<p>EBITDA results for the third quarter and nine months (in millions):  </p>
<p>				   Third Quarter	   Nine Months</p>
<p>				   1996    1995	  1996	1995</p>
<p>TIME WARNER</p>
<p>Publishing		    $ 99     $ 86	 $ 335   $   301</p>
<p>Music(a)			 143	 57	   454	 395</p>
<p>Cable			    122	 45	   352	  45</p>
<p>Time Warner EBITDA	   364	188	 1,141	 741</p>
<p>ENTERTAINMENT GROUP</p>
<p>Filmed Entertainment	 146	129	   423	 369</p>
<p>Six Flags Theme Parks(b)   ---	---	   ---	  60</p>
<p>Broadcasting, WB Network  (27)	(7)	  (63)	(40)</p>
<p>Programming -- HBO	    91	 74	   259	 220</p>
<p>Cable			    390	345	 1,134	 920</p>
<p>Entertainment Group EBITDA 600	541	 1,753     1,529</p>
<p>Combined EBITDA	  $   964    $ 729     $ 2,894   $ 2,270</p>
<p>(a) Includes pretax losses of $85 million recorded in the third quarter of 1995 related to certain businesses and joint ventures owned by the music division which were restructured or closed.</p>
<p>(b) Deconsolidated as of June 23, 1995, as Six Flags is now 49 percent owned.</p>
</text>
